        // storage write is disallowed. However the problem can be simplified: the property is about approvedToLog
        // returning approvedLoggers[_caller] — so for any address a for which approvedLoggers[a] is false,
        // both contracts return false. The distinguishing case is when approvedLoggers[a] is true. To create
        // such a case we will choose candidate as address(this) (the test contract) and exploit that we deployed
        // c; if C had set owner to msg.sender in its constructor it would be this test, but it didn't. To ensure
        // we can set mapping, we will call setApprovedLogger via a low-level call from an address that we make
        // into the owner by deploying a small OwnerSetter helper that calls setApprovedLogger as soon as it is
